  "description": "HUJWAM crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C99 H189 Cu3 Gd9 O55 P6 1-,C8 H12 Cu1 N4 1+. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1A (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1B (Cu) has 5 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 0 O neighbors; Cu3? (Cu) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.444-4.330 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.07-122.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cu(MeCN)4][Cu3Gd9(μ3-OH)7(O3PtBu)6(O2CtBu)15]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 7 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
